Angela Jean told me that they thought it would be really fun to offer this role to our longtime

1207
01:06:49.580 --> 01:06:51.900
casting director, Alison Jones.

1208
01:06:52.140 --> 01:06:53.480
But she said no.

1209
01:06:53.840 --> 01:06:54.880
She refused.

1210
01:06:57.100 --> 01:07:02.620
Greg wanted the incredible Beth Grant to play the role.

1211
01:07:02.920 --> 01:07:03.460
Well, yes.

1212
01:07:03.620 --> 01:07:07.040
Greg had worked with Beth before and knew her very well.

1213
01:07:07.040 --> 01:07:11.460
You guys might recognize her from the film No Country for Old Men.

1214
01:07:11.680 --> 01:07:13.340
I mean, she has a huge filmography.

1215
01:07:13.540 --> 01:07:16.380
But at this time, that film had just come out.

1216
01:07:16.800 --> 01:07:18.380
We reached out to Beth.

1217
01:07:18.760 --> 01:07:24.620
And she told us the story of exactly how she was cast on the show.

1218
01:07:24.620 --> 01:07:33.080
I was thrilled when I got the call to do this part and to be Rain's babysitter and girlfriend.

1219
01:07:35.100 --> 01:07:37.800
It's demented, and I love it.

1220
01:07:37.940 --> 01:07:42.560
And I had worked with Steve Carell fairly recently in Little Miss Sunshine.

1221
01:07:42.560 --> 01:07:46.580
So I was already completely in love with him and did love the show.

1222
01:07:46.580 --> 01:07:50.180
And I had worked with Greg Daniels on King of the Hill.

1223
01:07:50.180 --> 01:07:53.700
And we ran into each other during the Writer's Guild strike.

1224
01:07:54.000 --> 01:07:56.360
And I think he saw me in my strike mode.

1225
01:07:56.360 --> 01:08:00.320
I guess he knew I was right to be able to be that demented woman.

1226
01:08:02.760 --> 01:08:07.920
Well, then Beth shares with us what it was like to do the scene at the front door.

1227
01:08:08.060 --> 01:08:10.060
She's holding a cooler the whole time.

1228
01:08:10.180 --> 01:08:11.520
This is all happening.

1229
01:08:11.680 --> 01:08:14.120
It's her first scene of the episode.

1230
01:08:14.420 --> 01:08:15.660
Here's what she had to say.

1231
01:08:15.660 --> 01:08:21.000
Coming to the door to that dinner party was so thrilling for me.

1232
01:08:21.180 --> 01:08:23.360
It was so hard not to laugh.

1233
01:08:23.780 --> 01:08:27.160
I felt that since I knew Steve, he was out to get me.

1234
01:08:27.320 --> 01:08:28.560
He wanted me to break.

1235
01:08:28.740 --> 01:08:33.240
And here I was, a guest star, nervous with all you regulars, you fabulous comedians,

1236
01:08:33.560 --> 01:08:36.020
you brilliant comic minds.

1237
01:08:36.280 --> 01:08:39.180
And here I am, the guest star with Rain.

1238
01:08:39.440 --> 01:08:43.300
And opening the door is Steve Carell, just going for it.

1239
01:08:43.300 --> 01:08:48.840
And I started this riff and improvising to the point that I was determined not to laugh.

1240
01:08:48.920 --> 01:08:51.700
So I started almost grunting and crying.

1241
01:08:54.200 --> 01:08:58.800
I don't know if you can hear it in the episode, but, and tears in my eyes.

1242
01:08:58.860 --> 01:09:00.040
And he said, oh, great.

1243
01:09:00.200 --> 01:09:01.600
Now she's crying or something.

1244
01:09:01.740 --> 01:09:03.160
And I leaned over.

1245
01:09:03.320 --> 01:09:06.460
I was holding that cooler, you know, bringing our own food.

1246
01:09:06.460 --> 01:09:09.800
And since we weren't invited, holding that cooler.

1247
01:09:10.020 --> 01:09:13.560
And I leaned over, just shaking all over and came back up.

1248
01:09:13.660 --> 01:09:16.200
And somehow I think I managed not to break.

1249
01:09:16.340 --> 01:09:21.320
But that was the only time I managed not to break because you guys were just so hilarious.

1250
01:09:21.960 --> 01:09:27.940
Jenna, we should share with everyone what line Steve improvised that sent us all to the floor.

1251
01:09:27.940 --> 01:09:33.720
Yes, guys, Steve improvised the line, snip, snap, snip, snap.

1252
01:09:33.980 --> 01:09:38.500
You have no idea the physical toll three vasectomies has on a person.

1253
01:09:38.900 --> 01:09:45.700
I mean, you try not laughing with Steve Carell in front of you improvising stuff like that.

1254
01:09:45.880 --> 01:09:47.220
We were all a goner.

1255
01:09:47.520 --> 01:09:51.860
Well, it's interesting because Paul Feig sent in an audio clip about this,

1256
01:09:51.980 --> 01:09:53.420
and I'll let him explain it.

1257
01:09:53.520 --> 01:09:56.800
But there's a reason why Steve improvised that line.

1258
01:09:56.800 --> 01:09:57.760
Here you go.

1259
01:09:58.400 --> 01:10:01.520
There's so many great things to think about and remember from this episode.

1260
01:10:01.680 --> 01:10:05.460
But the one that makes me just realize how genius Steve Carell is,

1261
01:10:05.540 --> 01:10:08.260
in case anybody didn't realize that already,

1262
01:10:09.260 --> 01:10:12.960
is when the whole snip, snap run was,

1263
01:10:13.080 --> 01:10:18.220
it was a pretty dramatic scene of them, like, talking about having kids and all this.

1264
01:10:18.340 --> 01:10:20.320
And so we did several takes of it.

1265
01:10:20.420 --> 01:10:22.000
It was really good, but it was very dramatic.

1266
01:10:22.220 --> 01:10:24.000
And I remember kind of saying to Steve,

1267
01:10:24.800 --> 01:10:27.460
maybe let's do a take or just kind of find a little more humor in it.

1268
01:10:27.560 --> 01:10:30.020
I know it's kind of hard because it's kind of a serious subject.

1269
01:10:30.240 --> 01:10:31.380
And he's like, oh, okay, yeah, I get it.

1270
01:10:31.460 --> 01:10:31.660
I get it.

1271
01:10:31.700 --> 01:10:34.940
And that's when he did it, went off on the whole snip, snap, snip, snap,

1272
01:10:35.500 --> 01:10:36.420
which is just brilliant.

1273
01:10:36.580 --> 01:10:39.580
I mean, that scene is so funny because it's so heartbreaking and cringy,

1274
01:10:39.660 --> 01:10:40.760
but also hilarious.

1275
01:10:41.360 --> 01:10:43.080
I remember that, Angela.

1276
01:10:43.300 --> 01:10:48.360
I remember doing takes and takes of that scene where they were just going back and forth.

1277
01:10:48.560 --> 01:10:52.540
And you could just see the pain and Michael that he wasn't a father

1278
01:10:52.540 --> 01:10:55.520
and that Jan had been so manipulative of him.

1279
01:10:55.660 --> 01:10:57.240
And it was like a drama.

1280
01:10:57.480 --> 01:10:59.920
And then Paul came over and talked to Steve.

1281
01:11:00.300 --> 01:11:03.940
And they were like, how can we make this a comedy again?

1282
01:11:04.240 --> 01:11:07.620
How can we keep the dark elements of this scene,

1283
01:11:07.620 --> 01:11:09.900
but not let it get too heavy?

1284
01:11:10.400 --> 01:11:11.760
Brilliant Steve Carell.

1285
01:11:12.000 --> 01:11:14.340
Yeah, he so saves the moment.

1286
01:11:14.340 --> 01:11:15.400
And it's hilarious.

1287
01:11:15.700 --> 01:11:16.600
I mean, you're cringing.

1288
01:11:16.600 --> 01:11:17.460
It's horrible.

1289
01:11:17.680 --> 01:11:20.280
It's, but he makes it funny.

1290
01:11:20.980 --> 01:11:21.440
Yeah.

1291
01:11:21.720 --> 01:11:24.320
Well, now, guys, we're going to sit down at the table.

1292
01:11:24.580 --> 01:11:26.240
I guess dinner is ready.

1293
01:11:26.740 --> 01:11:27.580
Near ready.

1294
01:11:27.860 --> 01:11:28.340
Finally.

1295
01:11:28.920 --> 01:11:30.600
Can I point something out?

1296
01:11:30.880 --> 01:11:31.100
Yeah.

1297
01:11:31.360 --> 01:11:35.860
If you look at the table, we all have wine glasses, right?

1298
01:11:35.860 --> 01:11:42.000
We also all have water glasses, which are wine glasses.

1299
01:11:42.620 --> 01:11:50.360
So clearly Jan had more than six wine glasses because she is using them for water as well.

1300
01:11:50.500 --> 01:11:54.780
She just didn't want Dwight to come, you guys, to her fancy party.

1301
01:11:54.780 --> 01:11:56.940
He did not make the liSt.

1302
01:11:57.380 --> 01:12:00.180
Well, Dwight has started eating.

1303
01:12:00.500 --> 01:12:01.800
I mean, they brought their own food.

1304
01:12:01.960 --> 01:12:03.220
They're wasting no time.

1305
01:12:03.520 --> 01:12:05.020
They're the only ones eating.

1306
01:12:05.020 --> 01:12:08.420
Jan is still upset over what happened at the door.

1307
01:12:08.720 --> 01:12:10.900
She's so upset, she has to excuse herself.

1308
01:12:11.040 --> 01:12:11.920
She goes to the kitchen.

1309
01:12:12.260 --> 01:12:12.480
Yeah.

1310
01:12:12.700 --> 01:12:17.800
I mean, the last thing she said before she sat at that dining table was, I hate my life.

1311
01:12:18.380 --> 01:12:18.780
Yeah.

1312
01:12:19.100 --> 01:12:20.500
She's not in a good place.

1313
01:12:21.000 --> 01:12:26.780
Jenna, there's a deleted scene that is so fantastic where you kind of whisper to Michael,

1314
01:12:27.160 --> 01:12:27.900
go to Jan.

1315
01:12:28.180 --> 01:12:29.460
Go comfort her.

1316
01:12:29.700 --> 01:12:32.220
You kind of do this little motion, like, go say something.

1317
01:12:32.220 --> 01:12:35.020
So he gets up and he walks over to her.

1318
01:12:35.160 --> 01:12:40.200
Again, he's comforting her, but we're all witness to it.

1319
01:12:40.200 --> 01:12:44.120
And it's so clumsy and awkward.

1320
01:12:44.940 --> 01:12:47.240
And Sam, can you play the first part of that?

1321
01:12:48.320 --> 01:12:50.080
Hey, no, no, no.

1322
01:12:50.180 --> 01:12:50.740
Don't be sad.

1323
01:12:51.180 --> 01:12:51.980
Don't be sad.

1324
01:12:53.080 --> 01:12:55.460
Look, I care about you and I support you.

1325
01:12:59.620 --> 01:13:02.160
You are smart and beautiful.

1326
01:13:04.320 --> 01:13:06.300
And you have beautiful bosoMs.

1327
01:13:06.560 --> 01:13:09.500
And you can't even tell they're fake unless you're naked.

1328
01:13:11.400 --> 01:13:17.480
And I believe that with my support and your constant calls to Dr. Perry on my phone plan,

1329
01:13:17.700 --> 01:13:22.920
which is a little bit of a strain because I only have 20 anytime minutes a month.

1330
01:13:23.700 --> 01:13:25.840
Every minute after that is 75 cents.

1331
01:13:26.780 --> 01:13:30.520
Oh, you should look at some other plans.

1332
01:13:30.920 --> 01:13:32.740
Okay, thanks, weirdo.

1333
01:13:32.900 --> 01:13:33.580
But you know what?

1334
01:13:33.800 --> 01:13:36.060
I'm month to month because I don't want a two-year commitment.

1335
01:13:37.700 --> 01:13:42.340
I remember when he turned to Beth and goes, oh, thanks, weirdo.

1336
01:13:42.660 --> 01:13:44.300
We all lost it.

1337
01:13:44.860 --> 01:13:45.120
Yeah.

1338
01:13:45.840 --> 01:13:48.520
Gene said that's one of his favorite lines that got cut.

1339
01:13:48.760 --> 01:13:49.660
Oh, really?

1340
01:13:50.100 --> 01:13:50.520
Mm-hmm.

1341
01:13:50.520 --> 01:13:52.180
He loves that moment.

1342
01:13:52.820 --> 01:13:55.100
Michael continues to try to comfort Jan.

1343
01:13:55.560 --> 01:14:01.500
And it doesn't get any better, but it really paints a picture of how he feels about his home life with her.

1344
01:14:02.600 --> 01:14:03.940
What were you saying to Jan?

1345
01:14:04.300 --> 01:14:10.640
Honey, nobody in the complex likes you, but you have made this place look great.

1346
01:14:11.400 --> 01:14:12.760
It's like a museum.

1347
01:14:13.020 --> 01:14:13.300
Yeah.

1348
01:14:13.300 --> 01:14:23.580
You can't touch anything, which is a really strange way to feel in the place that you live.

1349
01:14:24.620 --> 01:14:28.100
You have made this home a house.

1350
01:14:29.660 --> 01:14:34.040
It's just what Paul Feig said about their design of the house.

1351
01:14:34.080 --> 01:14:34.700
Yes.

1352
01:14:34.880 --> 01:14:35.720
Like a museum.

1353
01:14:36.040 --> 01:14:39.420
You have made this warm, cozy home a house.

1354
01:14:41.260 --> 01:14:42.300
Oh, Michael.

1355
01:14:42.720 --> 01:14:52.720
I think they were right to leave those out because otherwise, I think we might have felt too badly for Jan when Michael is about to do what he's about to do.

1356
01:14:52.720 --> 01:14:54.580
But before we get there, Angela,

1357
01:14:54.840 --> 01:15:07.260
I have to talk about this moment when Dwight offers you some of his beet salad and you respond by saying the thought of popping one of his beets into your mouth makes you want to vomit.

1358
01:15:08.120 --> 01:15:11.460
Because I remember something else that was happening during this scene.

1359
01:15:11.560 --> 01:15:12.480
Will you share it with us?

1360
01:15:12.980 --> 01:15:13.180
Yeah.

1361
01:15:13.520 --> 01:15:21.320
It was actually really hard for me to focus in this scene and say my dialogue because Jenna, my daughter in my belly,

1362
01:15:21.600 --> 01:15:24.660
just decided in that moment she was going to run a full marathon.

1363
01:15:24.960 --> 01:15:28.500
She was like, digg-a-dick, digg-a-dick, digg-a-dick, kicking so much.

1364
01:15:28.640 --> 01:15:29.200
I don't know.

1365
01:15:29.280 --> 01:15:31.600
Maybe it's the sound of Rainn Wilson's voice.

1366
01:15:32.340 --> 01:15:37.460
Maybe Rainn's voice awoken my child in my womb and she was ready to fight.

1367
01:15:37.760 --> 01:15:47.140
But it was so surreal to me to be thinking about the timing of the scene and everyone's dialogue and when I was supposed to come in and trying not to laugh.

1368
01:15:47.340 --> 01:15:51.880
In the meantime, having this like wrestling match happening in my belly.

1369
01:15:52.120 --> 01:15:54.980
I think there are a lot of women who can relate to that, Angela.

1370
01:15:55.260 --> 01:16:00.080
I have a friend who is a lawyer and she was very, very pregnant and she was having to take a deposition.

1371
01:16:00.080 --> 01:16:02.780
And she told me at the end of the day, she was like,

1372
01:16:02.920 --> 01:16:14.460
I could barely focus on what I was doing because I was having to give very carefully worded questions and comments because it was all going on the record.

1373
01:16:14.620 --> 01:16:17.460
But all the while her kid in her belly was just tossing and turning.

1374
01:16:17.460 --> 01:16:19.980
Yeah, so much so.

1375
01:16:20.140 --> 01:16:23.520
And I have shared this story before and it's one of my favorite memories.

1376
01:16:23.840 --> 01:16:30.380
While the scene was going on, I'm talking, everyone is saying their lines and there's the rapid cadence of the dialogue.

1377
01:16:30.380 --> 01:16:44.440
I, off camera, grabbed Ed's hand and under the table, put it on my belly and he turned to me with his eyes wide and all of a sudden he wasn't Andy, he was Ed.

1378
01:16:44.600 --> 01:16:54.580
And he mouthed to me, oh my gosh, someone else to know and to witness like what I was like going through in the moment.

1379
01:16:54.580 --> 01:16:56.920
And it's such a special memory to me.

1380
01:16:57.020 --> 01:17:03.800
And when I rewatched the episode with my daughter, I said, Isabel, you were running a marathon in mommy's belly right now.

1381
01:17:03.920 --> 01:17:04.800
And she was like, what?

1382
01:17:05.380 --> 01:17:06.840
It's so special to me.

1383
01:17:07.300 --> 01:17:09.240
Guys, women are warriors.

1384
01:17:09.980 --> 01:17:14.820
We go to work and we focus on our work as if we don't have that going on.

1385
01:17:15.220 --> 01:17:22.140
Try to imagine how I could put it to a man like, OK, you're trying to give the most important presentation of your life.

1386
01:17:22.140 --> 01:17:25.120
And imagine a puppy is jumping at your leg the whole time.

1387
01:17:25.360 --> 01:17:28.180
Like, just the most distracting thing.

1388
01:17:28.540 --> 01:17:32.240
Jumping at your leg, but it's inside you, which is even weirder.

1389
01:17:32.760 --> 01:17:33.120
Yeah.

1390
01:17:33.400 --> 01:17:34.600
It's like the alien.

1391
01:17:34.600 --> 01:17:35.520
What is happening?

1392
01:17:35.900 --> 01:17:37.000
Women are warriors.

1393
01:17:37.580 --> 01:17:38.500
Way to go, Ange.

1394
01:17:38.980 --> 01:17:43.240
Beth Grant also shared her memories about shooting this dinner table scene.

1395
01:17:43.460 --> 01:17:44.560
Let's have a listen.

1396
01:17:45.060 --> 01:17:48.480
Sitting at that table and, you know, sucking on those beats.

1397
01:17:48.720 --> 01:17:51.540
The reason I was sucking on those beats was to keep from laughing.

1398
01:17:52.140 --> 01:17:57.520
And Rain's over there eating and going, mm, mm, mm, mm, mm, mm.

1399
01:17:57.640 --> 01:18:01.680
There's so much subtle humor in this episode.

1400
01:18:01.680 --> 01:18:05.540
And then, of course, the demented relationship that they have.

1401
01:18:05.680 --> 01:18:07.280
I love you all so much.

1402
01:18:07.280 --> 01:18:12.400
I'm so honored to be part of this very popular and respected episode.

1403
01:18:12.540 --> 01:18:17.500
Each of you doing such beautiful, subtle, hilarious comedy.

1404
01:18:17.500 --> 01:18:20.800
And I was so thrilled to see that all of you broke up, too.

1405
01:18:20.940 --> 01:18:25.280
Once we got inside and we sat down at the table and someone would break and say, sorry,

1406
01:18:25.480 --> 01:18:25.700
sorry.

1407
01:18:25.860 --> 01:18:26.960
And then someone else would break.

1408
01:18:27.160 --> 01:18:27.900
Sorry, sorry.

1409
01:18:28.060 --> 01:18:28.980
And then we'd keep going.

1410
01:18:29.280 --> 01:18:34.060
The last thing I'll say is when I came home, I said, I do not know how Paul is going to

1411
01:18:34.060 --> 01:18:35.060
edit this.

1412
01:18:35.500 --> 01:18:36.740
It's too hilarious.

1413
01:18:37.180 --> 01:18:39.180
Every moment is a three-hour episode.

1414
01:18:39.180 --> 01:18:41.240
I don't understand how he's going to do it.

1415
01:18:41.360 --> 01:18:43.060
But by golly, you did it.

1416
01:18:43.260 --> 01:18:50.200
And it is just an honor to have been part of this amazing, and as I say again, demented

1417
01:18:50.200 --> 01:18:51.200
episode.

1418
01:18:54.220 --> 01:18:55.540
Amazing and demented.

1419
01:18:56.620 --> 01:18:58.020
That sums it up.

1420
01:18:58.240 --> 01:18:58.380
Yeah.

1421
01:18:58.840 --> 01:19:04.500
Gene told me that he and Lee actually begged NBC to make this a supersized episode.

1422
01:19:04.500 --> 01:19:07.580
But I guess the schedule had already been set.

1423
01:19:07.760 --> 01:19:15.160
But he also told me that they did end up releasing a 29-minute producer's cut on iTunes that included

1424
01:19:15.160 --> 01:19:19.640
a bunch of deleted scenes, including some of the ones we talked about, like the granola

1425
01:19:19.640 --> 01:19:20.220
bar scene.

1426
01:19:20.420 --> 01:19:25.120
Maybe NBC didn't supersize it because they were holding a grudge because Greg wanted it to

1427
01:19:25.120 --> 01:19:25.960
go as is.

1428
01:19:26.600 --> 01:19:26.940
Ooh.

1429
01:19:28.740 --> 01:19:29.300
Wow.

1430
01:19:29.320 --> 01:19:30.840
I love that speculation.

1431
01:19:30.840 --> 01:19:35.660
They're like, no, you can have your weirdo episode, but it's only going to be 22 minutes.

1432
01:19:35.900 --> 01:19:37.040
We're not going to make it big.

1433
01:19:37.680 --> 01:19:38.900
That's what she said.

1434
01:19:39.180 --> 01:19:40.780
Oh, that's what she said.

1435
01:19:41.880 --> 01:19:47.600
One other little detail from this dinner party is how enormous the glasses were that Dwight

1436
01:19:47.600 --> 01:19:48.400
was drinking from.

1437
01:19:48.660 --> 01:19:51.280
To me, they look like glasses you buy at Spencer's Gifts.

1438
01:19:51.480 --> 01:19:55.840
Remember that place in the mall where you could get like kind of joke-sized stuff?

1439
01:19:56.180 --> 01:20:00.420
Well, Paul really loved these glasses, and there was one detail about them he wanted to

1440
01:20:00.420 --> 01:20:01.040
share with us.

1441
01:20:01.540 --> 01:20:06.900
One of my favorite gags in the show is when Dwight comes over with his babysitter and they're

1442
01:20:06.900 --> 01:20:08.360
at dinner with the wine glasses.

1443
01:20:08.360 --> 01:20:12.540
I had them fill the wine all the way to the top because I figured that's what Dwight would

1444
01:20:12.540 --> 01:20:15.460
think you would do with a big wine glass is you would fill it right to the rim.

1445
01:20:15.700 --> 01:20:19.700
So that's a little wine lover's joke for everybody.

1446
01:20:20.320 --> 01:20:22.320
You know what they look like to me, Angela?

1447
01:20:22.600 --> 01:20:28.780
They look like those wine glasses that I see a lot of moms post on Instagram about getting

1448
01:20:28.780 --> 01:20:29.560
through their day.

1449
01:20:30.080 --> 01:20:34.160
Wine weekend with the ladies and the wine glasses like the size of your head?

1450
01:20:34.420 --> 01:20:34.820
Yes.

1451
01:20:35.120 --> 01:20:36.620
That's what they remind me of.

1452
01:20:36.840 --> 01:20:37.080
Yeah.

1453
01:20:37.600 --> 01:20:39.400
Oh my God, lady, guess what?

1454
01:20:39.540 --> 01:20:39.880
What?

1455
01:20:40.220 --> 01:20:41.420
The food is ready.

1456
01:20:41.820 --> 01:20:44.200
The food is ready, but it might be poisoned.

1457
01:20:44.560 --> 01:20:45.440
Oh no.

1458
01:20:45.960 --> 01:20:47.400
Oh my gosh, yes.

1459
01:20:47.540 --> 01:20:53.540
Michael whispers to Pam, he thinks that Jan has maybe been trying to poison him.

1460
01:20:53.660 --> 01:20:55.680
He can't prove it, but he thinks.

1461
01:20:55.680 --> 01:20:58.780
He just hopes she didn't do anything to the food tonight.

1462
01:20:59.140 --> 01:21:00.580
Like what has been happening to Michael?

1463
01:21:00.720 --> 01:21:02.280
Has he been having violent diarrhea?

1464
01:21:02.740 --> 01:21:05.160
Stomach cramping after he eats with her?

1465
01:21:05.380 --> 01:21:07.440
Like what is making him think this?

1466
01:21:07.780 --> 01:21:09.520
Pam has a talking head.

1467
01:21:09.780 --> 01:21:11.360
Poor Pam is so hungry.

1468
01:21:11.640 --> 01:21:15.040
She says she knows that Jan did not poison the food.

1469
01:21:15.300 --> 01:21:22.500
But if she were going to poison the food, wouldn't she have poisoned Pam's since she is Michael's

1470
01:21:22.500 --> 01:21:23.200
former lover?

1471
01:21:24.280 --> 01:21:27.180
And now you know, Pam is not going to be able to eat.

1472
01:21:27.560 --> 01:21:29.600
You guys, Michael has soft teeth.

1473
01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:31.540
We learned that in this episode.

1474
01:21:32.020 --> 01:21:36.980
And because of his soft teeth, he has to dip his meat into his wine or probably whatever

1475
01:21:36.980 --> 01:21:38.340
beverage is in front of him.

1476
01:21:38.600 --> 01:21:40.940
And Jan hates it.

1477
01:21:41.320 --> 01:21:43.480
This has clearly come up before.

1478
01:21:43.900 --> 01:21:45.280
And she doesn't want him to do it.

1479
01:21:45.380 --> 01:21:46.460
She's like, could you stop doing it?

1480
01:21:46.560 --> 01:21:47.380
It's disgusting.

1481
01:21:48.120 --> 01:21:50.820
Lady, can I tell you a story about a guy I dated?

1482
01:21:50.820 --> 01:21:55.060
Oh, God, I was so worried you were about to tell me you dip meat into your beverages.

1483
01:21:55.060 --> 01:21:56.900
But it's about a different, it's a guy.

1484
01:21:57.420 --> 01:21:59.960
Angela, how long have you known me?

1485
01:22:00.160 --> 01:22:04.460
You thought maybe I dip my meat in beverages?

1486
01:22:04.700 --> 01:22:06.180
Well, you made a face.

1487
01:22:06.180 --> 01:22:07.640
You guys can't see her.

1488
01:22:07.780 --> 01:22:09.340
But she made a face.

1489
01:22:09.560 --> 01:22:13.120
You did the thing with your shoulders that you do, Jenna, when you're about to share

1490
01:22:13.120 --> 01:22:15.040
something with me that you haven't shared before.

1491
01:22:15.340 --> 01:22:18.380
And so I thought, oh, my God, I've eaten with her.

1492
01:22:18.460 --> 01:22:19.960
But have I ever eaten red meat with her?

1493
01:22:19.960 --> 01:22:20.620
Oh, my God.

1494
01:22:21.220 --> 01:22:23.120
No, I eat meat normally.

1495
01:22:23.300 --> 01:22:25.960
I can't believe that's a sentence I had to say.

1496
01:22:26.340 --> 01:22:26.560
Well.

1497
01:22:26.840 --> 01:22:27.500
But I did.

1498
01:22:27.780 --> 01:22:33.840
No, what I was going to share was I dated a guy who, first of all, had to drink milk

1499
01:22:33.840 --> 01:22:35.800
with every meal, not water.

1500
01:22:35.980 --> 01:22:36.340
Gross.

1501
01:22:36.560 --> 01:22:39.780
He was a grown man, but he had to have a big, tall glass of milk.

1502
01:22:39.940 --> 01:22:43.920
I mean, maybe no judgment, but I'm just saying, I don't know.

1503
01:22:44.180 --> 01:22:44.800
I judge.

1504
01:22:45.020 --> 01:22:45.740
OK, go on.

1505
01:22:46.060 --> 01:22:48.840
We're at a restaurant, orders a tall glass of milk.

1506
01:22:49.680 --> 01:22:57.800
But he had this thing where he would take a bite of food and then immediately take a

1507
01:22:57.800 --> 01:23:03.180
sip of milk and then chew the food with the milk in his mouth and then swallow it.

1508
01:23:03.380 --> 01:23:04.880
Oh, God.

1509
01:23:05.120 --> 01:23:08.760
And you had to sit and watch that through a whole meal?

1510
01:23:08.760 --> 01:23:12.840
Well, this was his preferred way of eating.

1511
01:23:13.120 --> 01:23:17.820
He liked the taste of his food mixed with a sip of milk.

1512
01:23:18.320 --> 01:23:19.540
All foods?

1513
01:23:20.440 --> 01:23:21.560
Every meal.

1514
01:23:21.820 --> 01:23:22.800
Every food.

1515
01:23:23.000 --> 01:23:24.740
A bite of sandwich, sip of milk.

1516
01:23:25.220 --> 01:23:27.340
A fork full of spaghetti, sip of milk.

1517
01:23:27.560 --> 01:23:28.820
That is disgusting.

1518
01:23:29.860 --> 01:23:31.440
That's a deal breaker for me.

1519
01:23:31.440 --> 01:23:37.540
I can't spend the rest of my life watching you take one bite, a swig of milk, and slosh

1520
01:23:37.540 --> 01:23:37.980
it around.

1521
01:23:38.140 --> 01:23:38.740
I can't do it.

1522
01:23:38.760 --> 01:23:39.080
I'm out.

1523
01:23:39.340 --> 01:23:40.940
I dated him a long time.

1524
01:23:41.080 --> 01:23:41.800
How long?

1525
01:23:42.100 --> 01:23:43.380
I don't want to say.

1526
01:23:43.500 --> 01:23:44.080
Oh, no.

1527
01:23:44.980 --> 01:23:45.800
Oh, no.

1528
01:23:45.940 --> 01:23:47.080
But it was a lot of meals.

1529
01:23:47.320 --> 01:23:49.000
A lot of milk meals.

1530
01:23:49.420 --> 01:23:49.940
Yeah.

1531
01:23:50.320 --> 01:23:56.320
Well, listen, Michael is really offended that Jan has pointed out this quirk in front

1532
01:23:56.320 --> 01:24:00.260
of the dinner party, and she is so evil.

1533
01:24:00.260 --> 01:24:02.120
She goes, oops.

1534
01:24:02.660 --> 01:24:03.640
And that's it.

1535
01:24:03.780 --> 01:24:04.780
Michael has had it.

1536
01:24:05.080 --> 01:24:07.620
He is going to take back his space.

1537
01:24:07.840 --> 01:24:09.220
He marches off.

1538
01:24:09.320 --> 01:24:11.280
We don't know where he's going or what he's getting.

1539
01:24:11.820 --> 01:24:15.900
While he's gone, I got a little glimpse of your plate, Angela.

1540
01:24:16.560 --> 01:24:16.900
Yeah?

1541
01:24:17.260 --> 01:24:19.440
Will you please tell people what you did?

1542
01:24:19.660 --> 01:24:24.080
You guys, it was one of those little actory moments, and it might also have been because

1543
01:24:24.080 --> 01:24:30.660
I was really pregnant and everything was smelling so strong to me, but I took my napkin, my fancy

1544
01:24:30.660 --> 01:24:36.360
napkin that Jan had laid out for all of us, and I just gently covered my meat with it so

1545
01:24:36.360 --> 01:24:37.940
I didn't have to look at it.

1546
01:24:38.160 --> 01:24:41.360
And I thought Angela Martin would do that because she's a vegetarian.

1547
01:24:41.560 --> 01:24:45.300
She wouldn't have eaten the meat or wanted to look at it, but she wasn't going to say

1548
01:24:45.300 --> 01:24:49.620
anything because this is clearly not the dinner party where you want to voice up about

1549
01:24:49.620 --> 01:24:50.220
the food.

1550
01:24:50.620 --> 01:24:53.020
So I covered my meat with the napkin.

1551
01:24:53.220 --> 01:24:54.000
So brilliant.

1552
01:24:54.080 --> 01:24:55.500
I love that choice.

1553
01:24:55.900 --> 01:25:02.540
Well, Michael comes back to the table, and he has brought with him his neon beer sign,

1554
01:25:02.540 --> 01:25:08.220
and he takes a painting off the wall, which, by the way, I want to point out is red, and

1555
01:25:08.220 --> 01:25:09.720
he hangs up his beer sign.

1556
01:25:09.980 --> 01:25:18.020
And when the neon light goes on, you hear the hum, and we are just bathed in this glow from

1557
01:25:18.020 --> 01:25:18.780
this sign.

1558
01:25:18.780 --> 01:25:24.900
Well, listen, it's a St. Pauli girl beer sign, and it's outlined in blue.

1559
01:25:25.200 --> 01:25:31.740
So when he turned it on, it was like a cascade of blue light filled the whole room.

1560
01:25:31.980 --> 01:25:33.420
It's just so incredible.

1561
01:25:33.420 --> 01:25:36.460
And you see the blue on Melora's face.

1562
01:25:36.640 --> 01:25:38.340
That's how bright the light is.

1563
01:25:39.080 --> 01:25:41.060
Jan is furious.

1564
01:25:41.800 --> 01:25:42.840
She gets up.

1565
01:25:43.100 --> 01:25:44.860
She turns on Hunter's CD.

1566
01:25:45.160 --> 01:25:48.660
And now we are going to have the argument.

1567
01:25:48.660 --> 01:25:53.880
Yeah, we thought we had the argument, but now the showdown is about to happen.

1568
01:25:54.220 --> 01:25:54.780
Yeah.

1569
01:25:55.100 --> 01:25:59.620
They start arguing about talent, about creativity.

1570
01:26:00.460 --> 01:26:03.280
Michael's like, I don't think he's a good singer.

1571
01:26:03.280 --> 01:26:05.140
I don't think he's very good at all.

1572
01:26:05.220 --> 01:26:06.920
But Jan seems to love him.

1573
01:26:06.920 --> 01:26:09.360
It's one of my favorite lines.

1574
01:26:09.860 --> 01:26:12.080
Jan says, at least he's an artiSt.

1575
01:26:12.300 --> 01:26:15.700
And Michael says, BFD, I'm a screenwriter.

1576
01:26:15.920 --> 01:26:18.020
And this is my favorite line.

1577
01:26:18.360 --> 01:26:23.480
Jan says, and I'm a candle maker, but you don't hear me bragging about it.

1578
01:26:24.260 --> 01:26:24.860
Yeah.

1579
01:26:25.020 --> 01:26:27.080
It's one of my favorite lines of the whole episode.

1580
01:26:27.700 --> 01:26:29.640
I also like this couplet.

1581
01:26:29.940 --> 01:26:32.360
You burn it, you buy it.

1582
01:26:32.540 --> 01:26:36.420
And then Michael says, great, I'll be your first customer.

1583
01:26:36.420 --> 01:26:38.740
You're hardly my firSt.

1584
01:26:43.910 --> 01:26:46.470
Believe, we got to sit in that room.

1585
01:26:46.730 --> 01:26:47.510
I know.

1586
01:26:47.870 --> 01:26:52.950
I mean, we got front row seats to this live show.

1587
01:26:53.250 --> 01:26:55.150
It was mind blowing.

1588
01:26:55.830 --> 01:27:01.850
Just the two of them were doing this dance and we got to watch it.

1589
01:27:01.950 --> 01:27:04.770
I am still blown away that we got to be there.

1590
01:27:05.170 --> 01:27:10.310
Well, when we asked Rainn Wilson about this episode, this is what he talked about.

1591
01:27:10.310 --> 01:27:23.170
I think the true hero of Dinner Party is the magnificent Malora Hardin, who is insanely brilliant all through the series, but especially in that episode.

1592
01:27:23.170 --> 01:27:36.630
I mean, Steve Carell being one of the all time greats on the planet Earth comedic actors and Malora Hardin stands toe to toe with him all the way through it being just as funny,

1593
01:27:36.810 --> 01:27:39.110
just as specific, just as weird.

1594
01:27:39.110 --> 01:27:52.150
And it's where you kind of see that Jan has turned a corner and that there is underneath this kind of external facade of blonde efficiency.

1595
01:27:52.150 --> 01:27:58.370
There is a very, very weird, egotistical, messed up human being under there.

1596
01:27:58.570 --> 01:28:00.530
Her candles, on and on.

1597
01:28:00.690 --> 01:28:03.270
But her performance is just magnificent.

1598
01:28:03.270 --> 01:28:04.610
It's so dry.

1599
01:28:04.610 --> 01:28:14.330
It stands the test of time as just one of the great all time performances all throughout the series, but especially in that episode.

1600
01:28:14.330 --> 01:28:19.970
When I rewatched it recently with my son, I was blown away by how great she was.

1601
01:28:21.070 --> 01:28:23.290
Malora is the star of this episode.

1602
01:28:23.490 --> 01:28:24.470
She just is.

1603
01:28:24.970 --> 01:28:25.270
Yeah.

1604
01:28:25.610 --> 01:28:27.930
We were so lucky to have her.

1605
01:28:27.930 --> 01:28:34.010
I mean, back on the pilot when we cast her, could we have known that this is what was going to happen?

1606
01:28:34.510 --> 01:28:43.870
Well, Jenna, Malora has shared with us that she felt like they knew the chemistry these characters could have if they really got room to run.

1607
01:28:44.030 --> 01:28:46.590
Way back on the pilot, here's what she had to say.

1608
01:28:46.770 --> 01:28:53.590
The whole Jan and Michael arc started when we were having lunch at the pilot episode.

1609
01:28:53.590 --> 01:28:57.870
Me and Steve and Greg were all having lunch together.

1610
01:28:58.150 --> 01:29:08.190
And somehow Steve and I both said, like, there was just some spark and some weird, dysfunctional attraction between Michael and Jan that if we ever got so lucky to make the series,

1611
01:29:08.190 --> 01:29:12.930
we would hope that we could get them to hook up somehow, some way at some conference or something.

1612
01:29:13.090 --> 01:29:14.470
So that was the beginning of it.

1613
01:29:14.470 --> 01:29:27.550
So I think going into it, I was always aware of what the potential for sort of showing this wonderfully complicated and dysfunctional relationship was the hilarity of that.

1614
01:29:27.730 --> 01:29:35.950
It was just so funny and so kind of dark, darkly funny, which just really appeals to my personal sensibilities.

1615
01:29:35.950 --> 01:29:42.710
I really loved that the dinner party took it to that next step of implosion.

1616
01:29:43.070 --> 01:29:44.230
Yeah, I was just thrilled.

1617
01:29:44.470 --> 01:29:54.370
I was just thrilled that we had a chance to really implode on screen in front of everybody and hopefully get a lot of laughs out of it, which we did.

1618
01:29:55.230 --> 01:30:10.230
Well, speaking of implosion, this whole thing is about to crescendo when Jan picks up a Dundee and smashes Michael's beloved plasma screen TV.

1619
01:30:11.430 --> 01:30:20.970
Yeah, I mean, he's like, back on your $0 salary, babe.

1620
01:30:22.210 --> 01:30:28.470
Oh, my favorite moment after that, there's the silence of like, oh, my God, what just happened?

1621
01:30:28.930 --> 01:30:34.730
And the person that calls it for the night that's like, yeah, I'm done here is Melvina.

1622
01:30:35.230 --> 01:30:37.010
She's like, yeah, I'm going to go.

1623
01:30:38.070 --> 01:30:41.290
Well, Melvina is the only person who doesn't work for this guy.

1624
01:30:41.290 --> 01:30:45.050
So she could be like, yeah, I'm out of here.

1625
01:30:45.250 --> 01:30:45.510
Yeah.

1626
01:30:45.790 --> 01:30:47.330
This is taking a turn for me.

1627
01:30:47.730 --> 01:30:52.110
Well, we had a fan question, Angela, from Meg, Emily, Ethan and Emma.

1628
01:30:52.110 --> 01:30:56.870
How many plasma screen TVs were broken by a Dundee?

1629
01:30:56.970 --> 01:30:59.770
And how many takes did this actually require?

1630
01:31:00.050 --> 01:31:06.830
Well, I reached out to good old Kentopedia, who told me that those little TVs were actually kind of expensive.

1631
01:31:07.170 --> 01:31:12.210
He said they bought five of them and we broke four.

1632
01:31:12.570 --> 01:31:21.070
Oh, now I remember doing a bunch of takes with Melora where she missed at first and they would have us react as if she hit it.

1633
01:31:21.070 --> 01:31:30.850
They could always use our reaction, but then she only had those five chances to actually land the Dundee when she was on camera.

1634
01:31:31.190 --> 01:31:35.590
And, you know, I mean, the sort of comical thing is it wasn't a big target.

1635
01:31:36.330 --> 01:31:40.990
It's a small thing to hit square in the middle with a Dundee.

1636
01:31:41.150 --> 01:31:42.070
It's true.

1637
01:31:42.450 --> 01:31:45.450
Well, we're all going to follow Melvina out the door, right?

1638
01:31:45.610 --> 01:31:46.990
Everyone gets up from the table.

1639
01:31:47.370 --> 01:31:48.050
They're going to leave.

1640
01:31:48.050 --> 01:31:53.990
I was actually asked not to get up from the table, if you notice, and it's because you would have seen my belly.

1641
01:31:54.130 --> 01:31:57.370
So I'm the last to leave the dining room.

1642
01:31:57.550 --> 01:32:00.610
Well, not only do we leave, but the police arrive.

1643
01:32:00.990 --> 01:32:03.930
There are two moments that are so delicious in the scene.

1644
01:32:04.290 --> 01:32:10.510
Well, one of my first things is right away the police officers are like, hey, Dwight, because they know him because he's always hanging around them.

1645
01:32:10.610 --> 01:32:12.130
He, like, wants to be part of the club.

1646
01:32:12.130 --> 01:32:22.870
And the other thing is, is when Michael says to them, as if they know what he's talking about, he says, my girlfriend threw a Dundee at my TV.

1647
01:32:23.490 --> 01:32:24.050
Yeah.

1648
01:32:24.490 --> 01:32:25.390
Can you imagine?

1649
01:32:27.410 --> 01:32:34.250
Well, they ask if he wants to press charges because some neighbors heard a lot of yelling, a big domestic disturbance.

1650
01:32:34.750 --> 01:32:37.630
And Michael says, I'll take the fall.

1651
01:32:37.810 --> 01:32:42.950
And they're like, no, you're actually not in fault.

1652
01:32:43.130 --> 01:32:44.750
You don't have to take the fall.

1653
01:32:44.990 --> 01:32:47.070
Is there anywhere you can go tonight?

1654
01:32:47.550 --> 01:32:47.810
Yeah.

1655
01:32:48.230 --> 01:32:55.970
And Dwight offers to take Michael home with him, which Michael refuses until he sees Jan come out of the condo.

1656
01:32:56.130 --> 01:32:57.210
And then he's like, yeah, yeah.

1657
01:32:57.330 --> 01:32:58.630
OK, no, I'll go home with you.

1658
01:32:59.250 --> 01:33:03.690
Well, Jenna, as everyone is leaving, there was a Dwight and Angela deleted scene.

1659
01:33:04.170 --> 01:33:07.770
And Angela is very sassy with Dwight.

1660
01:33:08.230 --> 01:33:09.350
I want to play it.

1661
01:33:10.030 --> 01:33:12.110
I noticed you're wearing open-toed shoes.

1662
01:33:13.350 --> 01:33:14.910
Since when did you become a whore?

1663
01:33:16.190 --> 01:33:18.990
There might be a lot of things about me that shock you.

1664
01:33:20.450 --> 01:33:23.950
Now, if you excuse me, I have to get back to my date.

1665
01:33:25.830 --> 01:33:28.490
There might be a lot of things about me that shock you.

1666
01:33:28.950 --> 01:33:34.150
And then I look him up and down, and I coyly kind of smile, and I walk away.

1667
01:33:36.510 --> 01:33:40.430
And now there's this series of scenes, right, that kind of wrap up the episode.

1668
01:33:40.430 --> 01:33:42.370
There's a montage of Jan.

1669
01:33:42.370 --> 01:33:44.270
She's trying to fix the Dundee.

1670
01:33:44.610 --> 01:33:46.790
You can tell she's sad.

1671
01:33:47.110 --> 01:33:49.730
She knows this night went horrible.

1672
01:33:50.390 --> 01:33:54.410
Clearly knows this is a night they might not come back from, right?

1673
01:33:55.030 --> 01:33:55.430
Yeah.

1674
01:33:55.890 --> 01:33:58.630
You see Jim and Pam having this really cute scene.

1675
01:33:58.730 --> 01:33:59.770
They finally got food.

1676
01:33:59.970 --> 01:34:00.790
They're having a hamburger.

1677
01:34:01.250 --> 01:34:01.850
Yes.

1678
01:34:01.850 --> 01:34:07.130
We got a fan question about this from Reagan Colliner, who wants to know what burger place

1679
01:34:07.130 --> 01:34:10.130
did Jim and Pam eat at the end because the burgers looked amazing.

1680
01:34:10.610 --> 01:34:12.650
I'll tell you what, the burgers were amazing.

1681
01:34:12.850 --> 01:34:17.890
I don't know if it was just because I'd spent four days saying I was hungry, but when I got

1682
01:34:17.890 --> 01:34:20.630
that burger, I'm really eating it in that scene.

1683
01:34:20.630 --> 01:34:21.790
I think you can tell.

1684
01:34:21.790 --> 01:34:24.830
I think you were happy to eat anything other than that granola bar.

1685
01:34:25.050 --> 01:34:26.290
I think I was.

1686
01:34:27.450 --> 01:34:35.150
Well, we filmed that scene at the Home Plate Burger Joint, and it was this little mom and

1687
01:34:35.150 --> 01:34:38.690
pop hamburger stand, which eventually, sadly, went out of business.

1688
01:34:38.690 --> 01:34:40.150
It's now a smog shop.

1689
01:34:40.310 --> 01:34:48.510
And in that same strip mall, there was a car wash that they turned into a Cold Stone Creamery,

1690
01:34:48.510 --> 01:34:53.790
and that is where Andy and Angela are sitting in the car having their ice cream.

1691
01:34:54.290 --> 01:34:54.650
Yes.

1692
01:34:54.950 --> 01:34:58.990
Ed and I have a very funny story about this moment, and I asked Ed.

1693
01:34:59.110 --> 01:34:59.710
I texted him.

1694
01:34:59.850 --> 01:35:03.050
I said, Ed, can I share about the car scene?

1695
01:35:03.230 --> 01:35:07.610
And he's like, yes, you can tell everyone I farted in the car.

1696
01:35:08.550 --> 01:35:12.770
So we're in the car, and he's supposed to lick a little bit of my ice cream, and then I

1697
01:35:12.770 --> 01:35:14.430
have to squish it on the side, right?

1698
01:35:14.630 --> 01:35:18.070
It took a few tries to get that squish just right.

1699
01:35:18.510 --> 01:35:22.690
And in between setting up, they'd have to clean the door, and we're in between setups,

1700
01:35:22.790 --> 01:35:24.850
and Ed had a little toot.

1701
01:35:25.090 --> 01:35:30.030
And I was really pregnant, as you guys know, and it smelled.

1702
01:35:30.030 --> 01:35:31.890
And I was like, oh, no, oh, no.

1703
01:35:32.390 --> 01:35:34.770
And we were rolling when it happened.

1704
01:35:34.910 --> 01:35:37.430
And so it's in the bloopers.

1705
01:35:38.150 --> 01:35:39.110
Here it is.

1706
01:35:40.410 --> 01:35:41.390
Oh, God.

1707
01:35:42.230 --> 01:35:43.190
Oh, God.

1708
01:35:43.970 --> 01:35:44.930
Oh, no.

1709
01:35:45.430 --> 01:35:47.670
If Angela's coming out of the car, I think I know what it is.

1710
01:35:47.670 --> 01:35:49.030
I'm sorry.

1711
01:35:49.470 --> 01:35:52.390
I didn't know what it is.

1712
01:35:52.630 --> 01:35:58.470
It's that bad.

1713
01:36:00.050 --> 01:36:02.290
He drove you from the car.

1714
01:36:02.510 --> 01:36:03.350
You had to get out.

1715
01:36:03.410 --> 01:36:04.970
I had to get out of the car.

1716
01:36:05.190 --> 01:36:09.290
And our crew was listening the whole time, and they were cracking up.

1717
01:36:09.430 --> 01:36:11.310
Ed is hitting the dashboard like, no.

1718
01:36:11.650 --> 01:36:12.730
No, come back.

1719
01:36:12.730 --> 01:36:13.530
I'm sorry.

1720
01:36:14.050 --> 01:36:15.810
It cracks us up.

1721
01:36:15.890 --> 01:36:17.090
It makes me laugh.

1722
01:36:17.090 --> 01:36:17.970
Oh, my gosh.

1723
01:36:18.550 --> 01:36:24.490
Years later, Jenna, when the show wrapped, Ed gave me the sweetest card.

1724
01:36:24.550 --> 01:36:28.410
He wrote all of these lovely things, and he ended it with,

1725
01:36:28.610 --> 01:36:31.870
and I farted in a car with you, so we'll always have that.

1726
01:36:32.150 --> 01:36:33.010
Love, Ed.

1727
01:36:37.910 --> 01:36:38.950
It happens.

1728
01:36:40.650 --> 01:36:49.450
Well, the very last scene is Dwight and Michael pulling up to this bus stop,

1729
01:36:49.550 --> 01:36:55.550
and as they pass by, we can see that Dwight's babysitter is waiting for the bus

1730
01:36:55.550 --> 01:37:00.110
with her cooler, and they do not offer her a ride.

1731
01:37:00.230 --> 01:37:01.570
It's terrible.

1732
01:37:02.330 --> 01:37:07.110
But Beth Grant sent in a little memory of shooting this as well.

1733
01:37:07.350 --> 01:37:12.050
I must say, at the end, when I'm standing at the bus stop waiting for the bus,

1734
01:37:12.250 --> 01:37:14.870
because he hasn't even had the decency to drive me home,

1735
01:37:15.010 --> 01:37:19.310
and his car pulls up, and we have this moment of looking at each other,

1736
01:37:19.510 --> 01:37:24.230
to me, is so esoteric and brilliant and wonderful.

1737
01:37:24.590 --> 01:37:28.850
And Raines looked to me, and then he drives off leaving me at the bus stop.

1738
01:37:29.890 --> 01:37:31.190
He's a free man.

1739
01:37:31.850 --> 01:37:36.750
I just love how tickled she is by her whole storyline in this.

1740
01:37:36.890 --> 01:37:40.410
She was so game for all of it, and I loved having her on set.

1741
01:37:40.550 --> 01:37:41.670
She was an absolute delight.

1742
01:37:42.490 --> 01:37:46.810
Yes, and Beth, oh my goodness, thank you so much for sending in these audio clips,

1743
01:37:46.830 --> 01:37:52.050
and thank you to Melora, and Rain, and John, and Ed, and Paul Feig,

1744
01:37:52.430 --> 01:37:57.930
Jean and Lee, Kintopedia, Jenna, everyone really showed up for us for this episode,

1745
01:37:57.930 --> 01:38:00.670
and Steve read the summary.

1746
01:38:01.010 --> 01:38:04.090
Guys, that's dinner party.

1747
01:38:04.410 --> 01:38:05.970
We hope you liked it.

1748
